  "current_contract": {
    "input": "The exact rational polynomials N8,Q2, integral coefficients and unit leading coefficient at the selected split primes.",
    "output": "The displayed unchanged N8 and Q2 are evaluated at w=Df(V_i)² for all current alternates and at the retained V0 value.",
    "transition": "At split71 for N and split7 for Q, integral roots contradict the nonroot reduction and negative-valuation roots contradict the unique unit-leading-coefficient term."
  },
  "evidence": {
    "path": "manuscripts/quartic_v14.tex",
    "sha256": "1f7bf748843d67c6a67d9863931ff0a15ca2548ae171ec1c1ce34b9002eb70a8",
    "start_line": 23340,
    "end_line": 23358,
    "excerpt_sha256": "cd78ea22ea188b04ddf7b054cfe6d2ab08517d4724196a72103cac70b235a56f",
    "text": "The larger auxiliary domain also requires global nonvanishing\nof the rational approximant numerator and denominator.\nIn its variable $w=Df^2$ their coefficient lists are\n\\[\n\\begin{split}\nN(w):\\;&1,-9776/5365,2941/3219,-1024/13949,\\\\\n &-1920/237133,-1024/711399,-1408/5928325,0,\n 2432/103152855,\\\\\nQ(w):\\;&1,-1526/1073,513/1073 .\n\\end{split}\n\\]\nThe unchanged certificates modulo71 for $N$ and modulo7 for $Q$\napply to every element of $K$. Both primes split in $K$; the\nrespective coefficients are integral, with unit leading\ncoefficient, and their reductions have no root. A root with\nnegative valuation is excluded by its unique leading term,\nand an integral root is excluded by reduction. Thus the old\nnonzero products and inverses remain justified. A positivity\ninterval restricted to doubled real points is not used here.\n"
  }
